    "prompt": "Create ONE production-ready transparent painted2D creature identity master for an ORIGINAL Heroes of Might and Magic III additional town, PILTOVER. No 3D model look, glossy game render, anime, vector, modern splash art, text or UI. Rich small-scale hand-painted sprite materials, compact readable contour, restrained highlights and dark textured outlines. Full creature silhouette large with substantial transparent margin, facing visually RIGHT in native HoMM3 three-quarter side view, top-left warm daylight. AERIAL SURVEYOR: living adult woman pioneer, visible human face, leather aviation goggles on forehead, navy fitted coat, ivory blouse, dark brown harness, short practical tied-back auburn hair; riding a LONG NARROW BRASS AND WOOD POWERED SURVEY FLIGHT BOARD. This is a small precarious experimental personal aeronaut platform with two modest blue-glass jet nozzles at its rear and delicate raised instrument mast, NOT an airplane, helicopter, hot air balloon, Corki, Zaun Firelight or superhero hoverboard. Her two feet stand apart in stirrup clamps on the deck; one hand holds a navigation control, other holds a long blunt grappling lance pointing frontward for melee. The long deck and lance form a readable low horizontal TWO-HEX outline. Fragile civilian survey equipment adapted for aerial skirmishing, not heavy armor. Physical navy pennant on aft mast bearing Piltover crest: central vertical spire and small orb with open circular horseshoe arc at lower stem, not wings. Brass, ivory, navy, muted brown, tiny restrained blue exhaust. No projectile gun, no magical wings. No scene, pedestal, huge glowing trail or cast shadow mat. Transparent background.\n",
